sts which i think is  something that is going to gain traction  as an idea uh uh following the way that  the  the government has behaved in recent  weeks and the longer this scandal goes  on the more  uh inclination there will be for the  government to reach for some big  dramatic thing to try and move the story  on and i think that would be a mistake i  mean and so i think that is the problem  we've got to deal with i think we also  need to  work out that i think that the one of  the crucial points that douglas makes is  parliament has now had powers returned  to it and i think what we've got to see  is that parliament is prepared to use  the powers that has had returned to it  and that parliament is prepared to  properly hold the executive  to account and parliament is prepared to  take more responsibility for its own  effect  by the way i know you said the last word  to james but can we just have a moment  also to observe like a minute silence  the complete horlicks that this  government is capable of making of  absolutely everything from the smallest  uh uh scandal to the biggest there is  nothing that number 10 at the moment it  doesn't seem to be capable of blowing up  into a huge storm it's quite remarkable  to watch  [Music]  you

